# 🌩️ ClauseGuard `.env` template

Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your keys.
Only `GROQ_API_KEY` is required to run locally.

```ini
# --- LLM (Groq) - required for analysis ---
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_xxx

# --- Optional: model selection ---
# mixtral-8x7b-32768 is decommissioned on Groq; gpt-oss-120b is the default.
PRIMARY_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
FAST_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
LLM_TEMPERATURE=0.2
LLM_MAX_TOKENS=4096

# --- Validation ---
MIN_TEXT_LENGTH=50

# --- Relational DB ---
# Dev default: SQLite at backend/data/clauseguard.sqlite3 (no config needed).
# Production: set a PostgreSQL URL
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host/dbname

# --- Authentication / JWT ---
# Generate with: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
# JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-64-char-random-string
# JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
# JWT_EXPIRES_MINUTES=1440
# When true, /analyze, /upload, /chat, /compare, /contracts, /history require a Bearer token.
# When false (default) the API stays open in guest mode with per-IP quota.
# REQUIRE_AUTH=false

# --- Optional: production persistence (set to enable) ---
# Redis for caching
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
# Firebase admin credentials (JSON path) for auth + cloud storage
FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS=./firebase-service-account.json
FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=clauseguard.appspot.com

# --- Vector store location ---
CHROMA_DIR=./chroma_db

# --- Business limits ---
FREE_TIER_ANALYSES_PER_MONTH=5
PREMIUM_PRICE_INR=500

# --- Uploads ---
MAX_UPLOAD_MB=10